Subject: [PATCH 0/6] mm/damon: add mTHP collapse and split control

This series extends DAMON with mTHP collapse and split control based on
access patterns.  It reuses the existing DAMOS_COLLAPSE action (merged
from Huawei) by adding a target_order field, and introduces a new
DAMOS_MTHP_SPLIT action with ARM SPE-based hot/cold detection.

Background
----------
DAMON provides data access monitoring but lacks proactive huge page
management.  khugepaged operates blindly (always try to collapse) and
has no split capability.  This series gives DAMON the ability to:

- Collapse small mTHPs (e.g. 16KB) back to PMD THPs (2MB) in hot
  regions identified by DAMON's access pattern monitoring.

- Split cold PMD THPs into smaller mTHPs, preserving only the hot
  subpages at the target order, reducing memory waste from partially
  hot THPs.

Architecture
------------
DAMON monitoring -> scheme filter -> COLLAPSE/SPLIT action

  damos_va_collapse()                damos_va_mthp_split()
  -> damon_collapse_folio_range()    -> damon_spe_hot_fraction()
  -> collapse_huge_page()            -> hot_pct < 80%?
                                          -> split_folio_to_order()

Collapse (patches 1-3):
  Reuses existing DAMOS_COLLAPSE action.  When target_order is 0
  (default), the existing madvise(MADV_COLLAPSE) path is preserved.
  When target_order is set, calls damon_collapse_folio_range(), a
  thin wrapper around collapse_huge_page() exported from khugepaged.

  No external mmap lock is held: collapse_huge_page() internally
  acquires and releases mmap locks; holding an outer mmap_read_lock
  would cause a self-deadlock.

Split (patches 4-6):
  Introduces DAMOS_MTHP_SPLIT action.  Uses folio_walk_start() to
  locate THP folios, queries damon_spe_hot_fraction() for sub-THP
  access heatmap.  THPs with >=80% hot subpages are preserved; colder
  THPs are split to the configured target_order.

SPE Feedback (patch 6):
  Three-phase architecture:
  - Phase 2a: PTE access bits via folio_walk (fallback, works everywhere)
  - Phase 2b: Userspace SPE daemon -> debugfs -> kernel rbtree
  - Phase 2c: Kernel-native ARM SPE event handler (future)

Test Results (ARM64 VM, 256MB anon random access, 60s)
-----------------------------------------------------
- Collapse:    nr_applied=10, sz_applied=69206016, AnonHugePages->67584kB
- Split:       target_order=2 (16KB), nr_applied=11, AnonHugePages->0kB
- Round-trip:  Split->Collapse, AnonHugePages 67584->0->67584
- Benchmark:   DAMON madvise +43.8% throughput vs baseline

Wang Lian (6):
  mm/damon: add target_order field for DAMOS_COLLAPSE
  mm/khugepaged: add damon_collapse_folio_range() for external callers
  mm/damon/vaddr: implement mTHP-aware DAMOS_COLLAPSE handler
  mm/damon: introduce DAMOS_MTHP_SPLIT action for mTHP split
  mm/damon/vaddr: implement DAMOS_MTHP_SPLIT handler
  mm/damon: add SPE feedback for sub-THP split decisions

